Package: structeval
Title: Structure-Aware Evaluation of Extracted Clinical Fields
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R:
    person("Max", "Moldovan", , "max.moldovan@adelaide.edu.au", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9680-8474"))
Description: Scores structured fields extracted from clinical notes against
    reference labels and reports precision, recall, F1, specificity and
    accuracy with intervals matched to each field's structure. Binary and
    scalar fields are note-level proportions and receive Wilson score
    intervals (Wilson 1927 <doi:10.1080/01621459.1927.10502953>). List fields
    yield ratios of note-level sums and receive a note-level cluster
    bootstrap with bias-corrected and accelerated percentiles (Efron 1987
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1987.10478410>) or a cluster-robust delta
    interval, with a stated rule at the boundary. Provides a threshold test,
    paired comparison tests, an omission-versus-commission asymmetry test,
    closed-form sample-size planners and Monte Carlo power from a generative
    model of clustered extraction errors.
